[h1]ZeD-GUI [B42] | tester build 0.2.0-t5[/h1]
[b]This is a test build.[/b] It is unlisted. Report problems in the pinned [b]Bug reports[/b] discussion, one post per problem.

ZeD-GUI replaces the inventory, the character and loot windows, the HUD and the menus for Build 42. The style is based on a 1993 Mac. It works with a controller and with a mouse and keyboard.

[h2]Before you subscribe[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Build 42 only.[/b] Tested on 42.21. It does not run on Build 41.
[*][b]Use a new game or a copy of a save.[/b] This is a test build.
[*][b]Tested in single player.[/b] It has not been tested in multiplayer. If you try it on a server, report what happened.
[*][b]It replaces the game's inventory and character windows.[/b] Buttons that other mods add to those windows do not show while ZeD-GUI is on. Mods that use the game's own systems (context menu options, container buttons, items, recipes) work.
[*][b]It adds one item:[/b] a steel digital watch in the loot. If you remove ZeD-GUI from a save, those watches are removed too. Everything else is interface and can be added or removed at any time.
[*][b]It comes with a helper mod, ZeD picks,[/b] which stays empty until you pick files in Mods.
[*][b]Text is in English.[/b] Where the game has a word, ZeD-GUI uses the game's translation.
[/list]

[h2]Windows[/h2]
[b]Character window.[/b] Tabs for loot, equipment, health, temperature, ID, journal, skills and the radio you carry. A walkie talkie is drawn as its own face, every knob and key working, and opens in full view.

[b]World window.[/b] Tabs for loot, crafting (at a bench or station near you), building, furniture, maps, foraging, animals, radios nearby (a ham set as its own face) and the vehicle you are next to. An oven or microwave shows its own control panel, and opens in a window of its own.

Open containers show as columns side by side. Either window's side panel can be rolled up into its title bar.

[b]Cards.[/b] Click an item, a generator, a campfire, a farm plot or a liquid for its card: what it is, what you can do, and why an action is not available.

[h2]HUD[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Belt:[/b] your hands, with a ring for the condition of what they hold, and the attachment slots of the gear you wear, on a strap drawn in the gear's material.
[*][b]Watch:[/b] a worn watch shows on the belt. Click it for the full watch: time, date, temperature, alarm and stopwatch.
[*][b]Dashboard:[/b] shows when you drive: the key turns, ash trays open, the taxi's meter runs, and the radio opens up close.
[*][b]Moodles:[/b] placed right, left or above the belt. A moodle's name and description show in a thought bubble when you point at it, and for a few seconds when it changes.
[*][b]Action bar:[/b] shows the current action and the queue in words, or as ten segments.
[*][b]Speech and thoughts:[/b] what your character says, and the action under way (Verbose action bar), show in bubbles over the head.
[*][b]Messages:[/b] notes from other mods go into one window instead of covering the game; errors are counted per mod for bug reports.
[/list]

[h2]Maps[/h2]
Three styles: survey, color and a paper road map. Flyers you have read are pinned on the map. Notes use the game's map notes, so they also show on the game's map.

[h2]Menus[/h2]
The main menu is a desk with a monitor. Load, new game, mods, options, sandbox, character creation and server settings open as windows on the monitor. They use the game's own menu functions.

[b]Mods.[/b] The list shows a mod that is missing a mod it needs or was made for another game version, and conflicts between mods: which copy the game uses, and why. A mod's info pane has tabs: About (what turning it off does to a save), Options (its own options, changed in place, and Reset settings), Sandbox (the settings it adds to a new game) and Conflicts. When two mods have the same code file, you can pick whose copy runs, file by file. Profiles save a mod list with its load order.

[b]Workshop.[/b] The Mod Uploader on the desk uploads your own mods from one window, with a description editor that shows the page the way Steam will.

[h2]Controller[/h2]
The controller scheme was designed by a player who plays on a controller.
[list]
[*]The D-pad moves between controls. A is left click, X is right click (the context menu), B backs out. Y opens and hides both windows; LB and RB pick one.
[*]With no window open, hold a D-pad direction for a wheel: Left is Character, Right is World, Up is Social, Down is Here and now. Point with the right stick and let go of the D-pad to take. A slice with more opens in place: A takes, B goes back.
[*]Hold Select for the ZeD wheel: theme, accent color, text size, UI scale, moodles, action bar, Messages, reset windows, ZeD setup and safe mode.
[*]Quick actions: in the world, hold LB or RB and press A, B, X, Y, L3 or R3 for one of twelve actions, set in ZeD setup or from a wheel.
[*]The buttons are drawn for your controller: Xbox, PlayStation, Steam Deck or Nintendo (ZeD setup, Gamepad glyph display).
[*]In the driver's seat the D-pad opens the wheels. World wheel, Vehicle, Dashboard gives the dashboard the controller.
[*]In a window, click the left stick to sort the list and the right stick to switch it between List and Grid.
[*]Aiming with the right stick hides both windows; Y shows them again.
[*]Camera zoom: hold LB and tap RB to zoom out, hold RB and tap LB to zoom in.
[*]Map: RT zooms in, LT zooms out. The left stick moves the cursor, and pushing it to an edge pans the map.
[*]If your Steam Input layout binds the bumpers to zoom, remove those bindings. ZeD-GUI handles the zoom itself.
[/list]

[h2]Options[/h2]
ZeD setup is the first page: dark, light or high contrast theme, nine accent colors, two text sizes and a UI scale (Auto picks it from the screen height). The quick actions and Put things back after an action are set here too. The game's own pages follow, and mark the settings ZeD-GUI replaces.

[b]Sandbox options in game[/b] (ZeD setup, Sandbox; off until you turn it on): change this save's sandbox settings from the pause window. Each setting says when a change takes effect and warns when it needs care. Single player only.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe.
[*]Main menu, Mods: turn on [b]ZeD-GUI[/b]. Put it after other interface mods in the load order.
[*]Quit the game and start it again. ZeD-GUI loads its fonts when the game starts.
[*]Start a new game, or load a copy of a save.
[*]Options, ZeD setup: set the theme, accent, text size, scale, moodle position and action bar.
[*]The inventory key opens the Character window. The loot key opens the World window. Controller buttons are the same as in the game.
[/olist]

[h2]Reporting a problem[/h2]
Post in the pinned [b]Bug reports[/b] discussion. Include:
[list]
[*]The version: 0.2.0-t5. It is shown in Mods, and in the desk's ZeD menu under About.
[*]Your game version and your mod list.
[*]What you did, what you expected, and what happened. Add a screenshot if you can.
[*]Your console.txt: [i]C:\Users\(you)\Zomboid\console.txt[/i] on Windows, [i]~/Zomboid/console.txt[/i] on Linux and macOS. The game replaces this file each time it starts, so copy it before you restart. Upload it to a paste site and post the link.
[/list]
[b]Safe mode:[/b] if ZeD-GUI stops you from playing, turn on Options, ZeD setup, Safe mode. The game's own screens return. Mention it in your report.
Play without the [i]-debug[/i] launch option unless asked. With it, the game stops on every Lua error, including errors from other mods.

[h2]Server admins[/h2]
Mod ID: ZeD_UI
Every player needs it, because it adds an item.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Made by Hermit. ZeD-GUI has been in development since Build 41 went stable. Every system, design and piece of logic was built to Hermit's vision. AI was used as a tool: Claude made it possible for one person to build a project that used to be out of scope for a solo modder. AI is the tool. Hermit is the maker.

Fonts: Fira Sans and Fira Mono (SIL Open Font License). Icons: sources and licenses are listed in the credits file.

Project Zomboid is made by The Indie Stone. ZeD-GUI is a fan-made mod built on the game's own systems, and is not affiliated with The Indie Stone or Apple.
